  "post_stream": {
    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 241591,
        "name": "Sea-Envy",
        "username": "Sea-Envy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/sea-envy/{size}/1849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-12-08T11:02:35.432Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I have had an idea for a little while now and with the new resources from the merger it might work. I figured I would bring it up here and if the community really likes it someone who has been in the same room as the GTG staff could mention it to them.</p>\n<p>GTG should sponsor Critical Roll pod cast to play a Sentinels RPG one shot.</p>\n<p>For those who do not know Critical Roll is a podcast / YouTube channel where pro voice actors play D&amp;D and other RPGs.<br>\nMost of the regular cast and some guest stars were casting picks for Sentinels characters when Christopher and Adam did voice casting for Sentinels.<br>\nThe Critical Roll cast are in art in the RPG main book attending the concert in the Battle of the Bands adventure (page 256)</p>\n<p>Secondary reason this would be the perfect reason for them to invite Colleen Clinkenbeard to Critical Roll.<br>\nColleen was also a voice pick by Christopher and Adam.<br>\nShe has ties to the superhero genre from acting and directing My Hero Academia<br>\nShe used to be roommates with Laura Bailey and is part of the “How did Laura meet Travis” story</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-12-08T11:02:35.432Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 9,
        "reads": 34,
        "readers_count": 33,
        "score": 96.8,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 28966,
        "topic_slug": "critical-roll",
        "display_username": "Sea-Envy",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
